	abstract = {By using positron annihilation spectroscopy methods, we have experimentally demonstrated the creation of isolated zinc vacancy concentrations {\textgreater}10(20) cm(-3) in chemical vapor transport ({CVT})-grown {ZnO} bulk single crystals. X-ray diffraction omega-rocking curve ({XRC}) shows the good quality of {ZnO} single crystal with (110) orientation. The depth analysis of Auger electron spectroscopy indicates the atomic concentrations of Zn and O are almost stoichiometric and constant throughout the measurement. Boltzmann statistics are applied to calculate the zinc vacancy formation energies (E(f)) of {\textasciitilde}1.3-1.52 {eV} in the sub-surface micron region. We have also applied Fick's 2(nd) law to calculate the zinc diffusion coefficient to be {\textasciitilde}1.07 x 10(-14) cm(2)/s at 1100 degrees C. The zinc vacancies began annealing out at 300 degrees C and, by heating in the air, were completely annealed out at 700 degrees C.},
